                                                "sense_id": "db4eb0f3-a57f-3f08-9ef0-32837ea77a2d",
                                                "text": "Tuna was carried down by the flood; and when Maui saw him in the net he stretched forth his arm and with a blow of his stone axe smote Tuna and cut off his head, and it and the tail fell into the ocean. ... The head became fish, and the tail became the koiro (ngoiro—conger-eel)."
